OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe 40th anniversary of the COW
OL,7,F(Computer-Originated World) globe saw
OL,8,Fit make an unexpected comeback.
OL,10,FA flashback sequence in EastEnders `
OL,11,Fwhich debuted the day after the iconic
OL,12,FBBC1 ident ` provided the perfect
OL,13,Fexcuse to dust it off.
OL,15,FIn modern terms, the introduction of
OL,16,Fthe COW was a rebrand of BBC One. It
OL,17,Fcame alongside major schedule changes
OL,18,Fdesigned to boost flagging ratings.
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,133,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13202
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F132A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G2/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FHowever it is worth remembering it was
OL,7,Fnot commissioned for this purpose. It
OL,8,Fwas the logical conclusion of a drive
OL,9,Fby Presentation over several years to
OL,10,Freplace models with computer graphics.
OL,12,FIt was a major infrastructure project.
OL,14,FSolid state devices were built for the
OL,15,Fnations and regions. The fact their
OL,16,Fident looked as good as network's for
OL,17,Fthe first time was a revelation.
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,133,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13203
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F132A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G3/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FWe know the devices were all installed
OL,7,Fbefore Christmas 1984 ready for a
OL,8,FJanuary start but the COW's
OL,9,Fintroduction was delayed until the new
OL,10,Flook schedule began in February.
OL,12,FSo given all this effort it is
OL,13,Fsurprising that a few inconsistencies
OL,14,Facross the network crept in.
OL,16,FMost obviously, there was the issue of
OL,17,Fhow to promote Ceefax subtitles.
OL,19,FThe network COW had an elegant caption
OL,20,Fwhich could be switched on and off as
OL,21,Frequired. It fitted the image
OL,22,Fbeautifully.
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,133,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13204
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F132A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G4/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FBut the nations were left to find their
OL,7,Fown solutions.
OL,9,FTheir Astons promoting subtitles were
OL,10,Finconsistent and sometimes looked
OL,11,Fclunky against the elegant ident.
OL,13,FCould a design solution not have been
OL,14,Ffound to provide a bespoke solution for
OL,15,Fthe nations?
OL,17,FWhile relatively few programmes were
OL,18,Fsubtitled in 1985, the proportion
OL,19,Fquickly grew.
OL,21,FThen there is the question of the clock
OL,22,Fdesign?
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,133,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13205
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F132A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G5/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhy did Cardiff and Glasgow have a
OL,7,Fclock with a blue centre dot, matching
OL,8,Fthe design of the previous network
OL,9,Fclock and the BBC Two clock?
OL,11,FNetwork's clock had the dot missing.
OL,12,FThis was also the case in Northern
OL,13,FIreland.
OL,15,FIt may not be coincidental that
OL,16,FNorthern Ireland's clock equipment was
OL,17,Fin use from the previous autumn and got
OL,18,Fupdated once the new look was
OL,19,Fintroduced.
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,133,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13206
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F132A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G6/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FWere Cardiff and Glasgow using an early
OL,7,Fdesign? And if so why was it not
OL,8,Fupdated?
OL,10,FOr was the "error" with network and
OL,11,FNorthern Ireland?
OL,13,FLook closely at the BBC One Wales COW
OL,14,Ftoo.
OL,16,FThe shading of the '1' is slightly
OL,17,Fdifferent to other versions?
OL,19,FWas this deliberate design? Or an
OL,20,Ferror?
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,133,120,200,300,0,100
PN,13207
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F132A1784184974
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}                 G7/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURESCReflections on BBC One's COW
OL,4,Cera on its 40th anniversary
OL,5,
OL,6,FGiven that the channel in Wales was
OL,7,Fstill known as BBC Wales ` not BBC One
OL,8,FWales ` was consideration given to
OL,9,Famending the design? The name did not
OL,10,Fchange orally until around 1988.
OL,12,FScotland had been using the name BBC
OL,13,FScotland since October 1983 but changed
OL,14,Fthe name back to BBC One Scotland when
OL,15,Fthe COW debuted.
OL,17,FFinally the way in which the nations
OL,18,Fmodified programme slides was
OL,19,Finconsistent. Did each nation just find
OL,20,Fits own way to amend the basic design?
OL,22,FIt's all fascinating.
OL,23,APub: 16-Feb-2025Qpppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,133,120,200,300,0,100
